# AURA â€” Product Requirements Document
**Version:** 1.1  
**Date:** April 2026  
**Status:** Draft  

---

## 1. Product Overview

Aura is a visually stunning, animation-rich music player web app built for personal and small-group use. It combines a cinematic landing page with a fully-featured player â€” no login, no signup, just open and listen.

Users load a local folder of songs and Aura handles everything: playback, visualization, synced lyrics, equalization, and library management â€” all wrapped in a dark glassmorphism interface powered by heavy Framer Motion animations.

---

## 2. Goals & Non-Goals

### Goals
- Deliver a uniquely aesthetic, animation-first music experience
- Allow instant use â€” no login, no account, no setup
- Support local folder loading with rich metadata display
- Ensure every song always renders poster art through a deterministic fallback chain
- Full audio controls: visualizer, synced lyrics, equalizer, shuffle, repeat
- Fast and smooth on PC/laptop browsers

### Non-Goals (v1)
- No mobile support
- No user accounts or cloud sync
- No paid streaming integration (Spotify, Apple Music)
- No social or collaborative features

---

## 3. Target Users

| Attribute      | Detail                                      |
|----------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Who            | Creator + small friend group (2â€“10 people)  |
| Device         | PC / Laptop (Windows or Mac)                |
| Browser        | Chrome, Firefox, Edge â€” latest versions     |
| Tech comfort   | Moderate â€” can open a folder, use a browser |
| Expectation    | Polished, fast, beautiful â€” not generic     |

---

## 4. Tech Stack

| Layer             | Technology                                                  |
|-------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| Framework         | Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript                        |
| Styling           | Tailwind CSS v3 + CSS custom properties                     |
| Animations        | Framer Motion (primary) + CSS transitions                   |
| Audio Engine      | Howler.js                                                   |
| Visualizer        | Web Audio API â€” AnalyserNode + Canvas                       |
| ID3 Tag Parser    | music-metadata-browser                                      |
| Lyrics            | LRCLIB API (free, no key, synced LRC)                       |
| Artwork Resolver  | Embedded ID3 art -> iTunes Search API -> Pollinations.ai fallback |
| State Management  | Zustand                                                     |
| Icons             | Lucide React                                                |
| Fonts             | Syne (headings) + DM Sans (body)                            |

### Why Next.js?
- File-based routing â€” each page is a clean route
- Built-in performance (image, font, code splitting)
- TypeScript out of the box
- Easy to add API routes later

### Preview Songs Recommendation
Use **Pixabay Music** (pixabay.com/music):
- 100% free, no attribution required
- Modern, high quality MP3s
- Come with metadata and album art
- Download 5â€“8 tracks and place in `/public/preview-songs/`

---

### v1 External API Plan

| Capability       | Provider          | Why it is locked for v1                                     |
|-----------------|-------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| Synced lyrics    | LRCLIB API        | Free, no auth, reliable enough for local-library playback   |
| Official covers  | iTunes Search API | Free, no key, strong catalog coverage, official album art   |
| Fallback posters | Pollinations.ai   | Zero-setup image generation when no embedded/official art exists |

**Implementation rule:** Aura should use embedded art on the client when available, then call a single artwork resolver endpoint for iTunes matching and AI fallback. This keeps provider logic centralized and easy to swap later.

